WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.668
-My first guest
is a very talented actor

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.871
that you know from his work in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:08.241
Now he is starring in the highly
anticipated new film "Cherry,"

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.143
which hits
select theaters Friday

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:13.346
and will be streaming on Apple
TV Plus starting March 12th.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.715
Here is Tom Holland.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.884
Tom, ah, it's great --
-Hey, Jimmy.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.819
-It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.054
Thank you so much.
-Thank you, mate.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.955
Nice to meet you, too.
-I'm a big fan.

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:25.024
I wish you could
be here in person.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:28.361
But I hear that you've
gotten very comfortable

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.197
doing virtual press, if you --

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.699
-Yes.
-Maybe a little too --

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.069
Maybe a little too comfortable.
I want to show you something.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:39.138
You posted this photo recently
of your virtual press look.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.239
It made me laugh.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.308
-Let's have a look.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.442
Oh, yeah.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:46.612
-That's -- Yeah.
It's only the waist up, man.

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:49.715
I thought that was --
I thought that was rad.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:53.285
And then Joe Russo, who --
the Russo Brothers,

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:55.421
who has directed you
in "The Avengers"

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:58.958
and your new film, "Cherry,"
decided to copy your look.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.060
Can we take a look at that?
-The thing that kills me

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.496
is that Joe's actually
got nicer legs than I do.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.630
-[ Laughs ] He does!

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.931
I looked at it, too.
-Look at his legs.

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:08.234
-Does he shave his legs,
you think?

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.436
-I don't know what he does.
I don't have to shave my legs,

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.339
because I'm like
a prepubescent teenager.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.208
I haven't grown hair
on my legs yet.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.143
Here, look, I'll just give you
a little glance.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.211
-[ Laughing ]
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:20.647
Holy mackerel.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.782
Oh, you're in big trouble
already, man.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.350
Hey, you know
what's interesting?

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.519
I was noticing --
You don't wear pants,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.388
but you do wear socks, though.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:31.257
-Yeah, 'cause it's cold,
and I --

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.359
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.196
Of course. Of course it is.
Yeah, I totally get it.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.131
-Because I got to wear
this suit jacket,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.766
and the suit jacket's too hot.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.835
-But I have my legs out,
'cause it's nice and freeing,

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.970
but then my toes get cold,
so I wear my socks.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.739
[ Chuckling ]
Toes get cold. Oh, my God.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.508
I know that you're in Atlanta

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.643
shooting the new
Spider-Man movie.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.545
And I know you can't
say much about it.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.580
But there are a lot of rumors
out there.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.781
Some people are saying

00:01:55.781 --> 00:02:00.186
that Jamie Foxx might be
coming back as Electro.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.654
No reaction.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:07.393
There's also a fan theory that
your Spider-Man predecessors,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.694
Tobey Maguire

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:09.996
and Andrew Garfield...
-Right.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.398
-...might be making a cameo
in this movie.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.034
You can't confirm or deny.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.635
-It would be amazing
if they were,

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:18.471
because they haven't
told me that yet.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.406
And I am Spider-Man,

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.242
and I've read the script
from the beginning to the end.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.445
So it would be a miracle if they
could have kept that from me.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.213
-Yeah.
-But at the moment,

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.615
there is no cameo
from the two boys.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:33.886
-But they do keep things
from you, though, don't they?

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.488
-Yeah, and actually,
it's getting to the point

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.390
where it's really frustrating.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.692
-Because I feel like now
I've progressed.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.195
I'm a trustworthy member
of the Avengers.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.231
And I haven't really ever
spoiled anything.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.833
-Mm.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.567
-Well, there's a few things,

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.102
but no big things.
-Wait, you actually have.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.171
You actually have.
-We'll leave it at that.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:56.976
-But there's one rumor that you
can exclusively confirm tonight.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.244
-Okay, go ahead.
-This will be the first

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.747
Spider-Man movie
with two Hollands in it.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:03.315
-Yes.
-Your little brother Harry

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:06.452
will be in the movie.
Is this correct?

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.920
-Yes, this is correct, yeah.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.524
-Who does he play,
and has he shot his part yet?

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.060
-Yes, in "Cherry," he has
a small cameo in "Cherry,"

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.862
and he plays a character
called the shaky kid,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.463
and he's a drug dealer.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.799
So we kind of had this idea
that in every film I would be in

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:24.503
that Harry would reprise
his role as the shaky kid.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.272
So he is back again

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:30.743
in his own sort of weird
MCU Cinematic Universe cameo

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.681
as the ecstasy-dealing
shaky kid.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.282
Yeah.
-Unbelievable.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.217
He's already being typecast.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.819
-I know. It's terrible.
Bless him.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.320
It must be really
difficult for him.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.688
-Is it fun, shooting
with your brother?

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.023
Do you pick on each other?

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.457
How does it work?

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.394
-It's interesting. In the scene,
he gets flipped upside-down.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.830
Spider-Man webs him upside-down,

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.298
and then he's
swinging back and forth

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.633
while I'm having an argument
with someone,

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.268
and he's kind of
swinging through frame.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.770
And I've obviously
done that for years.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.838
Being upside-down
is second nature to me now,

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:01.774
so I know how difficult
it can be.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.843
So at the beginning of the day,
I was, like,

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.779
making the takes
extra, extra long

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.281
just to see how long it would
take before he blacked out.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:10.483
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.851
-You're like,
"Can we do that one more time?

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.553
Just keep him swinging.
Keep him swinging back there."

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:14.787
-Yeah, I think I forgot my line.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.288
Like [bleep]
what was my line again?

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:20.125
Oh, that's right,
"I'm Spider-Man." And then --

00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:22.294
-That was the line.
Sorry. My bad.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.430
-I forgot. I thought
I was Batman for a moment.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.898
-I'm Spider-Man.
That's exactly correct.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.433
-But then towards
the end of the day,

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.869
I really did start
to get worried about him.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.137
And I was sort of
saying to the director,

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.939
like, "Listen, man,
we got to move on now.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.840
Look at him. He can
hardly speak anymore."

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.810
-He's blue, yeah.
-Yeah. Bless him.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.879
It's a funny scene, though,
and it was really fun for me

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.246
to get to share
that moment with him.

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:42.949
I'm sure my mum and dad
will be really proud.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.317
-That's cool, bud.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:47.620
One of the stages where
you're shooting "Spider-Man 3"

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.089
is actually the same place
that you originally auditioned

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.624
for the role of Spider-Man?

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.925
-Yeah.
-And I was just going to --

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.695
What was that like,
and in a weird way,

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:59.899
does it bring back flashbacks
of auditioning and going like --

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:03.569
'Cause I remember auditions, and
I never liked them.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.438
-Yeah, it's an interesting
feeling because I walk on-stage,

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:09.408
and I have that moment of panic,
of like, I haven't got my lines.

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:12.445
I'm going to ruin the audition.
I'm not going to get the part.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.280
And then I sort of
look back at my trailer,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.783
which is now way bigger
than it used to be.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.619
And I go, "Ah, I'm okay.
I'm on the third one.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.420
I'm fine. This is all good."

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.055
-Uh, yeah, exactly.
It's all good.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:26.358
I want to talk to you
about your new film, "Cherry."

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:27.660
You're incredible in this.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.861
-Thank you.
-Congrats.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.863
And it's already getting
all sorts of awards buzz.

00:05:31.863 --> 00:05:36.168
The movie is about
a lot of things.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:42.674
It's about war. It's about
addiction. It's about PTSD.

00:05:42.674 --> 00:05:44.243
Can you talk about why --

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:48.815
Why was it important for you
to tell this story?

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:50.849
-I think firstly, you know,

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:53.018
I needed to sort of educate
myself on the problem.

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:55.321
The opioid epidemic

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.456
wasn't something I knew
particularly very much about.

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.192
And I think one of my favorite
things about the film

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.327
is my character
doesn't have a name.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.528
And the reason
he doesn't have a name

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.363
is because it's not
the story of one person.

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:05.531
We're telling the story

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.066
of millions of people
around the world

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.835
who are suffering
from this problem

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:10.903
that is addiction and PTSD.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:13.538
So, for me, I wanted
to make this movie

00:06:13.538 --> 00:06:16.074
because I wanted
to help shed light

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:18.644
on a problem that is
on everybody's doorstep.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.380
It's seemingly invisible.
The battle against addiction

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:24.617
is one that always seems
to be fought in the shadows.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:27.953
So I hope that people
can watch this film

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:31.023
and feel more confident
about opening up, seeking help.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.191
I think seeking help

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:35.861
is something that people
should be heralded for

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:37.229
and congratulated,

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:38.964
saying that, "You've recognized
you've got a problem.

00:06:38.964 --> 00:06:40.633
You're seeking help,
and I'm really proud of you."

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.201
But unfortunately,
that isn't the case.

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:44.169
So I hope that this film can
really kind of

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:46.005
turn people's perspectives

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:50.109
on what it means to be an addict
and suffering from PTSD.

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:53.445
-In this movie, you --
It follows your character

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:55.748
through lots of
different phases,

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:59.752
including being a heroin addict.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:03.656
And I read that you lost
30 pounds to do those scenes,

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:07.026
and I heard that
it wasn't shot in order.

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:09.262
So you actually had to --
-No.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.798
-Why? Why not shoot it in order?

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:14.133
-I think that's just
the natural way

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.668
of doing an independent film.

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:18.437
You know, the schedule is always
going to be complicated.

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:20.206
-Yeah.
-The thing for me was that

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:22.441
we had a three-month period
before we started shooting

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:23.709
where I could lose the weight.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.177
We then shot
for about eight weeks

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:27.913
where I was doing the dope life
section of the movie

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:29.982
and obviously maintained
that weight loss.

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.618
And as we then went into the
chapters of him falling in love,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:35.254
him joining the Army,
him fighting in Iraq,

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.757
I could slowly
put the weight back on.

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:39.859
But during that part
of the film,

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:43.896
the Russos wrote this
new section for dope life,

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:48.200
which is the section
where my wife overdoses,

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.536
and I go to the car and have
that awful scene in the car.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:53.105
And I remember them
pitching me the idea.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.774
And I love the Russos.
I would do anything for them.

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:58.710
But I genuinely felt like
they were trying to kill me.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.113
Like, "I finished that.
I've put that to bed, man."

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.415
-You're like, "I just gained
all the weight back.

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:04.483
You're joking, right?"

00:08:04.483 --> 00:08:06.218
-Yeah, I was like,
"Is this a joke?

00:08:06.218 --> 00:08:08.353
Is someone filming me? Are you
trying to get me to flip out?

00:08:08.353 --> 00:08:09.755
What's going on here?"

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:13.259
But, yeah, no, so I had to start
trying to lose weight again.

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:14.660
And then we filmed
those three scenes.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.727
And I'm really proud we did.

00:08:15.727 --> 00:08:17.062
I think they really
help the film.

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:18.964
I think they help the narrative
of telling the story

00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:23.001
of how tragic the lives
of these people can be.

00:08:23.001 --> 00:08:25.471
But it was tough.
It was tough, to say the least.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.006
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:30.342
Here's Tom Holland in "Cherry."
Take a look.

00:08:30.342 --> 00:08:34.346
♪♪

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:37.216
-Have you seen bad things?

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:39.151
♪♪

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.287
-Yeah, a little.

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:44.223
-Are people getting killed?

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:45.791
Because I'm seeing on the news

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:51.063
that people are getting killed.

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.464
-[ Sobs quietly ]
-Hello?

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:55.300
-Yeah, baby, I'm here.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.438
-You're going to make it
through this, okay?

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:02.274
I know that you're going
to make it through this.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:04.476
♪♪

00:09:04.476 --> 00:09:07.245
-Could you just
talk about you for a second?

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:08.714
What's going on with you?

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:10.349
-Tom Holland, everybody.
When we come back,

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:13.252
Tom and I are going head-to-head
in a brand-new game.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:14.353
It's gonna be fun.
Stick around.

